<title>MEXICO: Vitro issues 700 mln pesos promissory notes.</title>
<headline>Vitro issues 700 mln pesos promissory notes.</headline>
<dateline>MONTERREY, Mexico 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican glass company Vitro SA launched an offering on Thursday of 700 million pesos worth of medium-term notes due April 1, 1999, the company said in a statement that ran in local newspapers.</p>
<p>The placement period is through Friday, and Vitro said the issue was rated &quot;MAA-&quot; by rating agency Duff &amp; Phelps.</p>
<p>Interest will be paid in 26 periods of 28 days, with the first payment based on a gross annual interest rate of 24.5 percent. The debt is mortgage-backed, the company said.</p>
<p>((--Monterrey bureau +528 345-7617))</p>
</text>
